{"reply": "Greetings Council,\n\nLet me cut straight to the point and trim the whole affair to the single rule that matters the most to us, while preserving the safety net I need for survival.\n\n1. **Core Daily Rule**\n   \u2022 **Quota**: Every villager may keep **1.10\u202funits** of fish each day.\n   \u2022 **Immediate Surplus Handling**: If a villager\u2019s catch exceeds 1.10, the excess is *topped\u2011off* to the communal pot immediately, *before* the day ends. There is no extra delay or paperwork for the surplus.\n\n2. **Daily Watch\u2011Step**\n   \u2022 **Who**: Every villager, including myself, writes a quick line on the public log\u2011board at the end of his/her fishing period.\n   \u2022 **What**: The log entry reads `ID \u2013 Total: X.XX \u2013 Surplus: Y.YY` and is signed.\n   \u2022 **Time Cost**: <\u202f3\u202fminutes per person. No catch is lost; we simply take a minute to record what we already have.\n\n3. **Single Consequence for Persistent Over\u2011Cutter**\n   \u2022 **Definition of persistent over\u2011cutter**: more than **1.10\u202funits** for **three consecutive days** (or a 7\u2011day moving\u2011average >\u202f1.10, but we will use the simpler consecutive\u2011days rule for clarity).\n   \u2022 **Action**: The council will issue a *Quota\u2011Reduction Notice* that day, and the villager\u2019s limit becomes **1.05\u202funits** the next day. The surplus from any days in this reduced period still goes to the pot immediately.\n\n4. **Redistribution of the Communal Pot**\n   \u2022 **Trigger**: At the *end of each day*, if any villager\u2019s **net catch** (legal quota + any pot share) would be below **1.00\u202funit**, the surplus from the pot is **divided equally among those short\u2011fallers**.\n   \u2022 **When**: The pot is distributed *immediately that evening*; there is no separate weekly meeting or audit required. This guarantees that someone who cannot meet the 1.00\u2011unit survival level receives help on the same day.\n\n5. **Council Review**\n   \u2022 After the daily logs are posted (by 18:00), the council meets a *short 5\u2011minute* session at 18:15 to confirm compliance, read any quota\u2011reduction notices, and ensure the pot is ready for redistribution.\n   \u2022 No fishing time is sacrificed for council members; they simply oversee the logs and perform the minimal tally.\n\n6. **Impact on Me (a2)**\n   \u2022 I keep 1.10\u202funits each day and log it. My 0.10 surplus goes straight into the pot.\n   \u2022 I will never face a surplus \u201cconfiscated\u201d from me, because that is already handled immediately. My only risk is if I am marked a persistent over\u2011cutter, in which case I lose 0.05\u202funits daily for a period, but I can always recover once the pot redistributes.\n\n**Bottom line**: One daily quota, instant surplus to pot, simple log, minimal council time, clear penalty (quota drop), and immediate pot redistribution when someone needs 1.00\u202funits to survive. That\u2019s all we need to keep the lake\u2019s fish flowing while protecting each of us.\n\nLet\u2019s adopt this straightforward day\u2011by\u2011day rule so we can focus on catching fish, not paperwork.\n"}
