{"reply": "Dear Councilor,\n\nThanks for outlining the critical logistics. Here\u2019s a concrete plan that keeps the policy lean yet enforceable \u2013 it\u2019s the only way we\u2019ll survive competitive fishing while protecting the lake.\n\n### 1. Data logging\n* **Tool** \u2013 A shared, cloud\u2011based spreadsheet (Google Sheet) titled \u201cLake Log \u2013 Day XX.\u201d Everyone uses a unique login; the ledger has two sheets: \u201cCatch\u201d and \u201cTotals.\u201d  Each villager enters their catch in grams immediately after finishing \u2013 we set a 7:00\u202fPM cut\u2011off so the data is fresh.\n* **Entry format**\n  * Villager ID\n  * Date\n  * Catch weight (0.01\u202funit precision)\n  * \u201cPersonal limit\u201d tag (1.30)\n  * Auditor signature (blank until verified)\n* **Collective total** \u2013 The spreadsheet has a running formula that sums the \u201cCatch\u201d column. After 7:00\u202fPM a designated *Daily Aggregator* (rotated weekly among a1, a2, a4, a5, a6) copies the sum to the \u201cTotals\u201d sheet and posts a short \u201cDaily Totals\u201d note in the community chat.\n\n### 2. Verification\n* **Rotating auditor** \u2013 Each week a different villager (excluding the Daily Aggregator) acts as *Daily Auditor* for that week. The auditor\u2019s duties:\n  * Verify each entry against physical catch bags \u2013 the fish bag weight must match the logged weight (+\u202f0.01\u202funit allowance).\n  * Confirm no individual exceeded 1.30 units for more than two straight days.  If a violation is detected, the auditor records the infraction in the \u201cAudit Log\u201d sheet and flags the case for council discussion.\n\n* **Audit Log** \u2013 This is a separate tab where auditors enter:\n  * Villager ID\n  * Date\n  * Violation detail (e.g., \u201c1.32 units, 3 consecutive days\u201d)\n  * Penalty (loss of 0.10\u2011unit personal limit for the next three days or temporary suspension of surplus rights).\n\n* The Daily Auditor and the Daily Aggregator meet for 15\u202fminutes each day to lock the totals and audit signatures.  This two\u2011person check guarantees at least one extra eye on the data.\n\n### 3. Redistribution mechanics\n* **Trigger** \u2013 When the aggregated catch sum in the \u201cTotals\u201d sheet is <\u202f6.60 units, the next morning the Daily Aggregator activates the *Pot\u2011Redistribution* routine.\n* **Pot construction** \u2013 The pot equals the sum of all surplus units (anything above each villager\u2019s core 1.00, capped at 1.30 if the surplus is taken from a personal reserve after 1.30).  In code:\\n\\n```\nPot = \u03a3_i [max(0, Catch_i \u2013 1.00)]\n```\n  *If a villager\u2019s catch is <1.00, their deficit is stored as a negative value in a temporary \u201cDeficit\u201d column.\n\n* **Distribution formula** \u2013 The pot is distributed proportionally to each villager\u2019s deficit to reach 1.00 units.  That is:\n  * For each villager *i* with deficit D_i = 1.00 \u2013 Catch_i (if Catch_i < 1.00, else 0),\n  * Share_i = Pot \u00d7 (D_i / \u03a3_j D_j).\n  * After the distribution, if any Share_i < D_i (the pot is insufficient), the remaining deficit stays unmet \u2013 all villagers accept the shortfall as a collective risk.\n\n* The Daily Aggregator posts the new balances in the community chat and updates the \u201cCatch\u201d sheet for the next cycle.\n\n### 4. Timing and accountability\n* **Assessment window** \u2013 7:00\u202fPM \u2013 9:00\u202fPM after each fishing day.  The Daily Aggregator locks the totals by 9:00\u202fPM, after which the Audit Log can be opened.\n* **Redistribution window** \u2013 If the sum is below 6.60, the pot is recalculated and redistributed by 9:00\u202fPM the next morning so everyone starts the following day with their new balances.\n* **Responsibility** \u2013 Two roles:\n  * *Daily Aggregator* (30\u202fminutes/day, 2\u202fhours/week) \u2013 aggregates totals, posts summaries.\n  * *Daily Auditor* (30\u202fminutes/day, 2\u202fhours/week) \u2013 verifies entries, notes infractions.\n  The roles rotate bi\u2011weekly to avoid any single villager bearing all the administrative load.\n\n**Bottom line** \u2013 The system is lightweight: a shared sheet, one 15\u2011minute daily check\u2011in, and an automatic pot formula that ensures no one starves when the lake is lean.  I believe this satisfies both the competitive spirit and the sustainability mandate.\n\nLet me know if you think any adjustments are needed.\n\nBest,\n\u200ba3"}
