| **Penalty specifics** | What is the exact penalty for a villager who exceeds 1.30 units on more than two consecutive days?  You mention “loss of 0.10‑unit personal limit for the next three days or temporary suspension of surplus rights.”  Which one applies?  If both are on the table, what are the precise thresholds that trigger each? |
| **Pot‑redistribution logic** | You compute `Share_i = Pot × (D_i / Σ_j D_j)` for those below 1.00.  What happens if the pot is **not** enough to fully cover the deficits (i.e., `Pot < Σ_j D_j`)?  Do the deficits simply stay unmet, or do you roll the remaining shortfall into the next day’s pot? |
| **Audit workflow** | The Daily Auditor verifies fish‑bag weights against logged entries.  What is the **acceptable variance** (e.g., 0.01 unit)?  If a bag is heavier than recorded, do you always flag an infraction, or is there a grace‑period if a missing digit explains the extra 0.01?  Also, how long will an infraction stay in the Audit Log before it’s reviewed by the council?  Is the audit log permanently retained or purged after a season? |
| **Time allocation** | You estimate 30 minutes/day, 2 hours/week per role.  Have you calculated how that time compares to the average fishing workload?  If a villager is forced to spend 2 hours/week on record‑keeping, do they lose that many hours of fishing on the water?  Would it be easier to automate the aggregation step (e.g., a Google Script that runs at 7:00 PM)? |
| **Role rotation** | The rotation is every bi‑week.  Is this schedule fixed or flexible (e.g., based on who was most present that week)?  If a villager is absent for an entire bi‑weekly period, how do we guarantee someone else covers both the Aggregator and Auditor roles?  One backup? |
| **Transparency** | The “Daily Totals” note is posted to the community chat.  Will that message be timestamped and stored in a permanent archive so that if a dispute arises later, we can look back at the exact posted total? |
| **Handling of lost sheets** | Since the log is in a shared sheet, how do we ensure that the sheet cannot be accidentally deleted or corrupted?  Is there a daily backup or version‑control snapshot of the spreadsheet? |

Answering these questions with concrete numbers and safeguards will give the council a clear, enforceable policy that is hard to circumvent and easy to audit."

