{"reply": "Dear Councilor,\n\nThanks for your precise questions. Here are concrete numbers and safeguards:\n\n1. **Penalties**:\n   * Threshold: any villager who logs >1.30\u202funits on **three consecutive days**, or records >1.32 on **any single day**, triggers a penalty.\n   * Penalty: the personal limit is reduced by **0.10\u202funits** for the next **three days**.  If the village repeats the violation during those days, the surplus\u2011rights are suspended for **one day**.  This provides both short\u2011term deterrence and longer\u2011term discipline.\n\n2. **Pot\u2011redistribution when insufficient**:\n   * Use the same formula: `Share_i = Pot \u00d7 (D_i / \u03a3D)`.  If `Pot < \u03a3D`, the residual shortfall `S = \u03a3D \u2013 Pot` is stored in a *Carry\u2011Over* column and added to the next day\u2019s pot.  Thus the pot can \u201cgrow\u201d on lean days.\n\n3. **Audit workflow**:\n   * Acceptable variance: \u00b10.02\u202funits (0.01\u202funit tolerance for scale drift).  >0.02 triggers an infraction.\n   * An infraction remains in the Audit Log until the council review at the **end of each 30\u2011day cycle**.  Logs are archived yearly for **five years**; otherwise they are purged at policy end.\n\n4. **Time allocation**:\n   * Current estimate: 30\u202fmin\u202f/daily per role.  With a Google\u2011Apps\u2011Script that runs at 7\u202fpm to auto\u2011sum totals, the Aggregator\u2019s time drops to **15\u202fmin** daily, while the Auditor stays at **30\u202fmin**.  This saves ~7.5\u202fh\u202f/\u202fweek per villager \u2013 about a 12.5\u202f% saving on a 6\u2011hour fishing day.\n\n5. **Role rotation**:\n   * Fixed bi\u2011weekly blocks.  A *backup* slot is assigned to the villager with the highest attendance that week.  If the primary is absent, the backup covers both roles.  If the backup is also absent, the schedule recedes to the next villager in order.  These assignments are logged in the \u201cRole Ledger\u201d sheet.\n\n6. **Transparency**:\n   * Each \u201cDaily Totals\u201d note posted to the community chat is automatically entered into the \u201cTotals Archive\u201d sheet with a timestamp.  Chat logs are stored read\u2011only in a shared Drive folder, ensuring an immutable audit trail.\n\n7. **Sheet integrity**:\n   * A daily snapshot is saved to a protected \u201cBackup Folder\u201d named `Lake Log \u2013 Day DD \u2013 YYYYMMDD`.  Google\u2011Sheets version history keeps all revisions for 30 days.  Only owners have edit rights; all formulas and ranges are locked for all others.\n\nI trust these specifics meet the council\u2019s need for enforceability while preserving our competitive spirit.\n\nBest,\n\na3"}
