h is deposited.\n   - If the daily catch is 1.10 or less, no fine is imposed. The fine applies only to the surplus portion above 1.10.\n\n4. **Re\u2011evaluation after the 7\u2011Day Period**\n   - At the end of the 7\u2011day penalty, the council will sum the daily total catches recorded in the ledger for those 7 days and divide by 7 to compute the average. If the average is \u2264\u202f1.10, the penalty is lifted and the villager\u2019s quota automatically reverts to 1.10 units.\n   - If the average is >\u202f1.10, the same 7\u2011day penalty will be reinstated, and the process repeats.\n\nThese procedures keep the workflow simple, rely on shared digital tools, and avoid cumbersome paperwork. I am ready to set up the shared sheet and schedule the first rotation.\n\nRespectfully, a4"}
