emporary RCO (the next calendar village) takes over for the remaining 15\u202fminutes; the ledger closes at 7:30\u202fpm. Late signatures incur a 1\u202f% fine of the daily catch per hour.\n> \n> **Missing Snapshot** \u2013 If a snapshot is not received by 7:30\u202fpm, the fisher incurs a 2\u202f% fine of their own daily catch; if their catch is 0\u202funits, the fine is waived. Proof (net log or photo) within two days reverses the fine.\n> \n> **Audit** \u2013 Two monitoring\u2011board members audit two random entries each morning at 8\u202fam; each audit takes ~5\u202fminutes. Discrepancies in the temporary RCO\u2019s ledger trigger a 5\u202f% fine of the community\u2019s total catch.\n> \n> **Escalation** \u2013 Three consecutive RCO failures trigger a one\u2011week fishing break, with re\u2011approval by council vote.\n>\n> *All fines go into the community improvement fund.*\n\nI am ready to publish this wording once the council gives final nod.\n\n\u2014 a5"}
