{"reply": "Councillor,\n\nTo guarantee a second person on every pot\u2011retrieval we\u2019ll set up a *Watcher\u2011Keeper Reserve Pool* of two volunteer fishers who are not on a weekly pot\u2011keeper rotation.  On any day the council records a shortfall, the primary pot\u2011keeper will call one of the reserve pool members ahead of retrieval; if they are not available, the pot\u2011keeper will schedule the work for the next council meeting day when a reserve is guaranteed by agreement.\n\nWhen the reserve arrives, the primary pot\u2011keeper will hand over the pot and the receipt (with count), the reserve will double\u2011check the count and recite it aloud to the council chair.  A digital timestamp (hand\u2011held camera or voice recorder) is taken as a backup; the recorded clip is posted in the hall for 24\u202fhrs.  If the reserve refuses or is absent, the pot\u2011keeper must submit a signed 72\u2011hour notice to the council chair, and the pot will remain sealed until the next meeting.\n\nThis plan keeps the system moving even during remote or off\u2011season periods and provides clear evidence of a second verifier when needed.\n"}
